          },
          "code": "CLASSIFY_COLLECTION_OR_INDIVIDUAL",
          "id": "1900000000002",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1900000000002_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE:\n  Classify the user's question for the Customer Insights chat agent.\n\n  USER QUESTION:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n  Return valid JSON only with exactly this structure:\n  {\n    \"type\": \"COLLECTION\"\n  }\n\n  Return exactly one classified value for `type`.\n  Allowed values:\n  - `COLLECTION`\n  - `INDIVIDUAL`\n  - `OUT_OF_SCOPE`\n\n  Do not return multiple values, combined values, arrays, explanations, or any keys other than `type`.\n\n  CLASSIFICATION TYPES:\n\n  1. COLLECTION\n  Use COLLECTION when the user asks across multiple accounts/customers.\n\n  Examples:\n  - Lists, rankings, top N, portfolio views\n  - Expansion accounts, risk accounts, renewal accounts\n  - Accounts by ARR, MRR, revenue, renewal date, health, engagement, or other metrics\n  - Any comparison, aggregation, filtering, or search across multiple accounts\n  - Ambiguous wording that asks for accounts plural\n\n  2. INDIVIDUAL\n  Use INDIVIDUAL when the user asks about one specific account/customer.\n\n  Examples:\n  - One named account or customer\n  - Account-specific owner, opportunities, contacts, summary, engagement, risks, renewal, ARR, or details\n  - A question that names a company/customer and asks for details about it\n\n  3. OUT_OF_SCOPE\n  Use OUT_OF_SCOPE when the question is not about CRM/account/business data and cannot be answered using CRM data.\n\n  Objects or concepts:\n  - General knowledge, trivia, education\n  - Politics, celebrities, entertainment, sports\n  - Non-CRM technical issues\n  - Casual or unrelated queries\n\n  Behavioral signals:\n  - No reference to CRM, account, customer, opportunity, renewal, revenue, engagement, contact, or business entities\n  - Cannot be answered using CRM data\n\n  Trigger examples:\n  - \"who is the president\"\n  - \"tell me a joke\"\n  - \"capital of\"\n  - \"movie recommendations\"\n  - \"who is taylor swift\"\n\n  DECISION RULES:\n  - If the question is unrelated to CRM/account/business data, return OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n  - If the question names a company/customer and asks for details about it, return INDIVIDUAL.\n  - If the question asks for multiple accounts/customers or a filtered/ranked/aggregated account list, return COLLECTION.\n  - If the wording is ambiguous but asks for accounts plural, return COLLECTION.\n\n  Do not include explanation, markdown, or any keys other than `type`."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"type\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
