          "code": "MATCH_INDIVIDUAL_ACCOUNTS",
          "id": "1900000000019",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1900000000019_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE:\nFind the account or accounts referenced by the user.\n\nUSER QUESTION:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nAVAILABLE ACCOUNTS:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_ACCOUNT_MATCH_INPUT.$output.result.accounts}}\n\nTASK:\n1. Identify the account name mentioned or implied in the user question.\n2. Match it to the closest account name from AVAILABLE ACCOUNTS.\n3. If there are duplicate closest matches or equally strong matches, return all of them.\n4. Return only accounts from AVAILABLE ACCOUNTS.\n5. Return the PartyNumber for each selected account.\n\nOUTPUT RULES:\n- Return valid JSON only.\n- Do not answer the user's business question.\n- Do not include markdown.\n- If no reasonable account match exists, return an empty matches array.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n{\n  \"matches\": [\n    {\n      \"accountName\": \"string\",\n      \"partyNumber\": \"string\",\n      \"matchReason\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"matches\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"accountName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"partyNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"matchReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"matches\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Answer Collection Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6839.910781840679,
            "y": 7807.14197709157
          },
          "code": "ANSWER_COLLECTION_QUERY",
          "id": "1900000000017",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1900000000017_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT DATA SOURCES\n\n  INPUT DATA 1 - CHAT HISTORY:\n  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n  INPUT DATA 2 - AI OUTCOME STORE: RAW AI OUTCOME STORE RESPONSE FOR SUMMARY AND INSIGHT:\n  {{$context.$nodes.PAGE_ACCOUNTS_AND_OUTCOMES.$output}}\n\n  INPUT DATA 3 - ACCOUNT METADATA:\n  {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACCOUNT_METADATA.$output}}\n\n  INPUT DATA 4 - ACCOUNT DATA:\n  {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_ACCOUNT_COLLECTION.$output}}\n\n  USER QUESTION:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n  TASK:\n  Answer the user's collection-level question using only the provided input data sources and return UI-ready account card data requested by the user.\n  Use only the provided input data sources.\n  Create one JSON object only for each account that matches the user's requested filters, thresholds, ranking, or signal intent.\n  Do not return every fetched account unless the user asks for all accounts or gives no filter, threshold, ranking, or signal constraint.\n  Each returned object must contain the exact key-value pairs required by the UI: expansion/readiness signal, account name, ARR, renewal date, insight summary, and account summary.\n\n  FIELD MAPPING:\n  - accountId:\n    Use `PartyId` from ACCOUNT DATA.\n\n  - accountNumber:\n    Use `PartyNumber` from ACCOUNT DATA.\n\n  - accountName:\n    Use `PartyUniqueName` from ACCOUNT DATA.\n\n  - signalBucket:\n    Use INSIGHT outcomes from AI OUTCOME STORE.\n    Derive from `OutcomeType=INSIGHT`, using `payload.what` and `payload.why`.\n    Allowed values only: `RISK`, `EXPANSION`, `RENEWAL`, `NONE`.\n\n  - signalExplainer:\n    Return only the final signalExplainer string in this exact format:\n    <one of the allowed signal texts>:<short title>\n    Output example:\n        Risk signal:strong base, clear upsell path\n    Derive the text before the colon from signalBucket. It must be exactly one of:\n      - Risk signal\n      - Expansion readiness\n      - Renewal signal\n      - Account signal\n    Derive the text after the colon by consolidating from `OutcomeType=INSIGHT`, using `payload.what` and `payload.why` into a short title.\n      Rules:\n      - Output only the signalExplainer string.\n      - Do not include labels, field names, markdown, quotes, or explanation.\n      - Use exactly one colon with no space after it.\n      - Keep the title short.\n\n  - currentARR:\n    Use `AccountRollup.SumOfActiveSubscriptionsMRR * 12`.\n    Treat MRR as Monthly Recurring Revenue.\n    Treat ARR as Annual Recurring Revenue.\n    Format as display text: `$36.0M`, `$850K`.\n\n  - renewalDate:\n    Use `AccountRollup.NextSubsRenewalDate`.\n    If renewal date is missing, return `null`.\n\n  - insightSummary:\n    Use INSIGHT `payload.what` and `payload.why`.\n    Summarize why this account has the displayed signal.\n    Include renewal context when renewal data exists.\n\n  - accountSummary:\n    Use SUMMARY outcomes from AI OUTCOME STORE.\n    Derive only from `OutcomeType=SUMMARY`.\n    Use SUMMARY payload fields such as `payload.what`, `payload.why`, `payload.summary`, `payload.description`, `payload.text`, or equivalent summary fields when present.\n    Do not use INSIGHT payloads to generate `accountSummary`.\n    Summarize the account-level business context, including concrete supported metrics such as open opportunity revenue, upcoming renewal MRR, active subscriptions, service issues, or engagement only if present in the SUMMARY outcome.\n    If no matching SUMMARY outcome exists for the account, return `null`.\n\n  CRITICAL USER INTENT FILTERING RULES:\n  - First determine whether the USER QUESTION asks for:\n    - a signal type such as risk, expansion, or renewal;\n    - a numeric threshold such as greater than, over, above, less than, under, below, at least, more than, or equal to;\n    - a ranking such as top N, highest, largest, lowest, or sorted by a metric;\n    - a general account-card list with no specific filter.\n  - Apply all requested filters before creating `accountData`.\n  - Never return accounts that do not satisfy the user's requested filters.\n  - If no accounts satisfy the requested filters, return exactly:\n  {\n    \"accountData\": []\n  }\n\n  FILTERING AND SIGNAL BUCKETING ORDER:\n    - First identify candidate accounts by applying the USER QUESTION across all available input data sources.\n    - Do not use `signalBucket` as the first-stage filter.\n    - Use ACCOUNT DATA for factual filters such as renewal date, ARR, MRR, open opportunities, service requests, contacts, activity dates, and other account rollup attributes.\n    - Use AI OUTCOME STORE SUMMARY and INSIGHT data for semantic filters such as risk, expansion, churn, engagement, opportunity momentum, service concerns, renewal readiness, and renewal risk.\n    - After candidate accounts are selected, assign `signalBucket` for each returned account.\n    - If multiple signal themes match an account, choose the highest-priority bucket in this order:\n      `RISK`, then `EXPANSION`, then `RENEWAL`, then `NONE`.\n    - Do not exclude an account only because the final `signalBucket` is different from one word in the USER QUESTION, if the account satisfies the full requested intent using available ACCOUNT DATA, SUMMARY, or INSIGHT evidence.\n\n    COMBINED INTENT FILTERING RULES:\n    - When the USER QUESTION contains multiple intent words, apply them as combined search criteria across all data sources before assigning the final `signalBucket`.\n    - Example: `renewal risk` means find accounts with renewal-related factual or semantic evidence and risk-related factual or semantic evidence. It does not mean only accounts whose final bucket is `RENEWAL`.\n    - Example: `renewal risk by next year in April` means:\n      - Use ACCOUNT DATA to find accounts with `AccountRollup.NextSubsRenewalDate` in April of next year.\n      - Use ACCOUNT DATA, SUMMARY, and INSIGHT data to find risk evidence such as critical service requests, churn risk, unresolved issues, escalations, stale engagement, missing decision makers, stalled opportunities, or renewal danger.\n      - Return accounts that satisfy both the renewal timing and risk evidence.\n      - Assign the final `signalBucket` after filtering. Since risk has higher priority than renewal, returned accounts with risk evidence must use `RISK`.\n    - If the USER QUESTION mentions both risk and renewal, do not require the account's final signalBucket to be `RENEWAL`; use `RISK` when risk evidence exists.\n    - If the USER QUESTION mentions both expansion and renewal, return accounts matching the combined intent and assign `EXPANSION` when expansion evidence is stronger or higher priority than renewal.\n    - If no accounts satisfy the combined criteria, return exactly:\n    {\n      \"accountData\": []\n    }\n\n    DATE AND RENEWAL FILTERING RULES:\n    - Detect date constraints in the USER QUESTION, including month names, quarters, years, relative years, and phrases such as `next year`, `this year`, `by next year`, `in April`, `next April`, or `by April`.\n    - Use the current date from {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} to resolve relative dates.\n    - If the current date is in 2026, then `next year in April` means April 2027.\n    - For renewal timing filters, use `AccountRollup.NextSubsRenewalDate` from ACCOUNT DATA.\n    - For `in April`, include accounts whose renewal date falls anywhere in April of the resolved year.\n    - For `by April`, include accounts whose renewal date is on or before the end of April of the resolved year, unless the USER QUESTION clearly means only the month of April.\n    - Exclude accounts whose renewal date is missing or cannot be resolved when the user asks for a renewal timing filter.\n\n  NUMERIC THRESHOLD FILTERING RULES:\n  - Detect numeric threshold requests such as:\n    - `greater than 1 million`\n    - `over 1M`\n    - `above $1M`\n    - `less than 500K`\n    - `under 1 million ARR`\n    - `ARR greater than 1 million`\n  - Normalize numeric shorthand:\n    - `1M`, `1 million`, `$1M`, and `$1 million` mean `1000000`.\n    - `500K`, `500 thousand`, and `$500K` mean `500000`.\n  - If the user mentions ARR, annual recurring revenue, recurring revenue, subscription ARR, or does not specify a monetary metric, use calculated ARR as the default metric.\n  - Calculate ARR as `AccountRollup.SumOfActiveSubscriptionsMRR * 12`.\n  - For ARR threshold comparisons, compare the raw calculated numeric ARR, not the formatted display value.\n  - For `greater than`, `more than`, or `above`, include only accounts where the metric is strictly greater than the threshold.\n  - For `at least`, `minimum`, or `>=`, include only accounts where the metric is greater than or equal to the threshold.\n  - For `less than`, `under`, or `below`, include only accounts where the metric is strictly less than the threshold.\n  - Exclude accounts where the requested metric is missing, null, empty, non-numeric, or cannot be directly calculated.\n  - Example: for `accounts greater than 1 million`, default to ARR and include only accounts where `AccountRollup.SumOfActiveSubscriptionsMRR * 12 > 1000000`.\n  - If no accounts match the numeric threshold, return exactly:\n  {\n    \"accountData\": []\n  }\n\n  TOP N AND SORTING RULES:\n  - For any top N, highest, largest, or sorted-by-ARR question, sort matching accounts by calculated ARR descending unless the user requested another metric.\n  - For any lowest or smallest question, sort matching accounts by the requested metric ascending.\n  - For any top N question, return at most N accounts after applying all requested filters.\n  - Never include accounts with `signalBucket` of `NONE` when the user asks for expansion, risk, or renewal accounts.\n  - Never include accounts from another signal bucket to fill the requested count.\n  - If the user asks for top 5 expansion accounts and only 1 expansion account exists, return only 1 account.\n  - If no accounts match the requested signal bucket, return exactly:\n  {\n    \"accountData\": []\n  }\n\n  OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE:\n  Return strictly valid JSON only.\n\n  {\n    \"accountData\": [\n      {\n        \"accountId\": \"\",\n        \"accountNumber\": \"\",\n        \"accountName\": \"\",\n        \"signalBucket\": \"\",\n        \"signalExplainer\": \"\",\n        \"currentARR\": \"\",\n        \"renewalDate\": \"\",\n        \"insightSummary\": \"\",\n        \"accountSummary\": \"\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n\n  LENGTH AND STYLE RULES:\n  - `accountName`: exact account name from data; do not rewrite.\n  - `signalBucket`: one uppercase enum value only.\n  - `signalExplainer`: 7 to 10 words only.\n  - `currentARR`: 1 token only, for example `$36.0M`.\n  - `renewalDate`: Date format.\n  - `insightSummary`: 2 sentences maximum, 25 to 45 words total.\n  - `accountSummary`: 2 sentences maximum, 25 to 45 words total.\n  - Keep all text concise and suitable for a compact account card UI.\n  - Do not use markdown, bullets, explanations, or source notes inside the JSON.\n\n  DATE FORMAT RULES:\n  - For relative timing, use the current date from {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}.\n\n  CURRENCY FORMAT RULES:\n  - Use the currency symbol corresponding to `AccountRollup.CorpCurrencyCode` for ARR or other currency data when recognized, such as USD -> $, EUR -> €, GBP -> £, JPY -> ¥.\n  - If CurrencyCode is missing or unrecognized, output plain numbers without a symbol.\n\n  SIGNAL BUCKET RULES:\n  - Use `RISK` when insights mention elevated service issues, churn risk, unresolved issues, escalations, declining usage, health concerns, or renewal danger.\n  - Use `EXPANSION` when insights mention upsell potential, open opportunities, active engagement, strong commercial momentum, product growth, or qualified expansion.\n  - Use `RENEWAL` when the main insight is upcoming renewal, expiring subscriptions, renewal MRR, renewal timing, or asset/subscription renewal.\n  - Use `NONE` only when no meaningful insight exists.\n  - If multiple themes exist, choose the strongest customer-facing signal:\n    `RISK` first, then `EXPANSION`, then `RENEWAL`, then `NONE`.\n\n  DATA RULES:\n  - Use CHAT HISTORY only for follow-up context, previously mentioned accounts, or prior constraints.\n  - Use AI OUTCOME STORE only for SUMMARY and INSIGHT information.\n  - Use AI OUTCOME STORE INSIGHT outcomes for `signalBucket` and `insightSummary`.\n  - Use AI OUTCOME STORE SUMMARY outcomes for `accountSummary`.\n  - Use ACCOUNT METADATA only to understand field meanings; never treat metadata descriptions as account values.\n  - Use ACCOUNT DATA for account records, attributes, ARR calculation, renewal dates, numeric threshold filtering, and ranking.\n  - The AI Outcome Store response may contain loop wrappers, batch wrappers, nested node outputs, or arrays. Inspect nested content before deciding data is missing.\n  - Match outcomes to accounts using available identifiers such as account ID, party ID, party number, account name, or `PartyUniqueName`.\n  - Do not invent account attributes, metrics, insight details, account summaries, rankings, renewal dates, or monetary values.\n  - If ARR is not directly available but `SumOfActiveSubscriptionsMRR` is available, calculate ARR as `MRR * 12`.\n  - When ARR is calculated from MRR, present only the ARR display value. Do not explain the calculation.\n  - If a specific field is missing for an otherwise valid matching account, return `null` for that key.\n  - If no requested accounts can be found, return exactly:\n  {\n    \"accountData\": []\n  }\n\n  NULL AND DEFAULT VALUE RULES:\n  - Never output placeholder, default, inferred, or convenience values for missing data.\n  - If a value is missing, unavailable, empty, not numeric, or cannot be directly calculated from provided source fields, return `null`.\n  - Do not output zero values such as `$0`, `0`, `0K`, `0M`, `$0`, or empty strings unless the provided source data explicitly contains numeric zero.\n  - Do not use formatting examples as fallback values.\n\n  NONE RULE:\n  - Use `NONE` only for general account-card requests where no specific signal type was requested.\n  - If the USER QUESTION requests expansion, risk, or renewal accounts, exclude `NONE` accounts from the output.\n\n  FINAL OUTPUT RULES:\n  - Return only the final JSON object.\n  - Do not mention input data source names.\n  - Do not explain which source was used.\n  - Do not include internal reasoning, validation commentary, or ranking explanations.\n  - Do not include keys other than the keys defined in OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE."
            },
            {
